    "narrative": "The Austin Waves carry a high-ceiling lineup into today\u2019s slate, anchored by **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.11), who represent our strongest offensive plays. **Cole Carrigg** benefits from an optimal intersection of a favorable park and a vulnerable matchup against Ray, while **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start despite the lingering uncertainty of a \"Lineup Pending\" status; his ability to thrive in neutral platoon splits makes him a must-start regardless of his final slot. **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) and **Andy Pages** (69.99) also offer significant upside, with **Heliot Ramos** capitalizing on a massive 6.43 xERA matchup and **Andy Pages** positioned to exploit the slow delivery of Wandy Peralta to potentially manufacture stolen bases, our primary objective for the category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves the benching of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.46), who fell just shy of cracking the starting nine. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** possesses a high base projection, the combination of a daunting matchup against Logan Gilbert and a negative park factor pushed his efficiency below the threshold established by **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Lowe**. We are closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Liam Hicks**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages**; should any of these players move down significantly in their respective batting orders, their dynamic scoring will require immediate re-evaluation. While **Jackson Merrill** holds a respectable 53.21, we have flagged him as a risk given the elite skill of Yoshinobu Yamamoto, making him the most susceptible to a mid-game swap if his efficiency wanes.",
